    "judgment": "REC-104 reproduced a production metadata-loss boundary: CTE and query-composition paths could discard enum descriptors, set-operation output schemas did not reconcile nominal identity and nullable carriers, and null-extended, aggregate and generated-row shapes could lose the descriptor at lowering. The fix keeps enum identity and source-read metadata in logical output schemas and generated shapes, rejects same-carrier different-identity set operands with MQ3109, rejects enum/ordinary carrier conflicts with MQ3110, and preserves original query spans through subquery-to-CTE diagnostics. Streaming set-operation arm names are collision-aware so repeated source aliases remain unambiguous. No row-value inspection or primitive-carrier identity inference was introduced."
  },
